// firewall.dw with the PERMIT removed -- the forbid alone, which is how three of the five policies
// in examples/aws2 are written as individual files.
//
// Cedar is default-deny, so on its own this grants nothing at all: every request `firewall.tla`
// names is refused, and `OutsideIsRefused` holds without testing anything. That is what
// `--decision-probe` exists to catch, and it is not hypothetical -- five drafted properties out of
// five failed exactly this way on a real policy set, and only mutation scoring noticed, one TLC
// run per mutant, to conclude "it survived every mutant".
forbid (
    principal,
    action == Anchor::Action::"Connect",
    resource
)
when { context.input.origin == "external" };
